<title>JAPAN: Japan March crude imports fall 5.2 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan March crude imports fall 5.2 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) issued the following data on crude oil imports during March 1997:</p>
<p>CRUDE OIL   (1,000 kl) (1,000 bbl) mth/mth% yr/yr%</p>
<p> Iran	   3,316	 20,858    - 0.2    +37.1</p>
<p> Saudi Arabia 5,318	 33,450    +12.8    + 4.3</p>
<p> Kuwait	 1,367	  8,598    - 1.2    +16.0</p>
<p> Neutral Zone 1,241	  7,806    +26.8    - 8.4</p>
<p> Qatar	  1,631	 10,259    + 1.0    -18.6</p>
<p> Oman	     925	  5,818    -21.6    -33.6</p>
<p> UAE	    6,016	 37,841    + 5.7    - 6.9</p>
<p> Yemen	    142	    893     - 0.6   +71.8</p>
<p> China	  1,037	  6,523     - 7.5   -17.7</p>
<p> Malaysia	 444	  2,793     +46.4   -11.5</p>
<p> Brunei	   258	  1,623     - 9.1   -40.0</p>
<p> Indonesia    2,062	 12,970     +56.3   +20.9</p>
<p> Vietnam	  532	  3,346     +20.6   - 3.1</p>
<p> Mexico	   159	  1,000     +21.8   -72.5</p>
<p> Gabon	    105	    660     -19.3   + 3.2</p>
<p> Australia	 43	    270     -75.2   -60.6</p>
<p> TOTAL	 24,594	154,696     + 5.9   - 5.2</p>
